A||||13||ChadMan||Whupped good by a Celica GT-S||||9||
Z||000000||ChadMan||06-21-2001||01:36 PM||||Got on 315 North to head home for lunch and all three lanes were going 60 in a 65.  Right to left: tow truck, moving van and Dodge minivan in the passing lane (of course).  Lots of cars stacked up behind them.  <P>The next ramp we come to has an entrance lane about 1/4 mile long and no one is merging on or off the freeway, so I use that lane to pass the whole logjam of cars and continue on my way at about 75 mph.  (Oooo...I'm a daaaaangerous driver!)<P>About three miles up the road I check my rearview and a brand-new Celica GT-S is bearing down on me pretty good.  Now normally I'd just let him go, but visibility is excellent and I'm feeling squirrely, so I downshift and gun it.  But it's not even close...he slows down to about 90, gives me the Hawaiian "hang loose" sign (fist with thumb and pinky out), then floors it, and man, he's gone.<P>I could have pursued it and tried to hang with him, but why?  I'm beaten already.  (And I have a feeling pursuing a losing cause is how most street-race crashes happen.)<P>I think it would have taken a 3.4 or a NOS-ized 2.8 to beat him.  I guess being a Duke driver is like being a Cincinnati Bengals fan...you'd better savor your victories because they're few and far between.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 06-21-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000001||firstfiero||06-21-2001||01:49 PM||||        I've beaten the stock gt more then once but those gts's are fast! I haven't gone up against one yet but by the numbers my v6 doesn't stand a chance. <P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">         <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||88formula||06-21-2001||05:17 PM||||As I was reading your story I was thinking you had a v6.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jay||06-21-2001||06:55 PM||||I raced a brand new GTS on the highway a few weeks ago.  He kept up to my 300 horses pretty good.  BTW it was raining, just a light drizzle, you know when it's real slippery.  We got up to about 110mph and I passed him, then I decided that was enough.  I don't need to loose my license or my life to prove a point.  They are increadibly quick cars. Who would have thought?  I rarely race on the street, too dangerous, not worth it.<P>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||06-21-2001||09:46 PM||||Don't feel bad, 88Formula.  As I was WRITING my story I was WISHING I had a V6!||||reg||10
Z||000005||Fformula88||06-21-2001||09:52 PM||||Sounds like you caught him at the worst time possible too.  Those engines make their big power north of 6000 RPM.  On the highway its easy to downshift and get those RPM's.  From a standstill, they are a little sluggish off the line.  Thats not to say they are slow, but the highway is where those cars will really shine!  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||saleenfiero||06-21-2001||10:07 PM||||Yeah, they can barely even spin their tires off the line, but combine that friggin 180 horse VTEC, with the close ratio 6 speed and you have quite a car.  I used to like em, but now they are twelve for ten cents around here, no big deal anymore.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fyerstarter||06-21-2001||10:14 PM||||Actually "V-TEC" is only found in Honda motors. But I know what your saying. Toyota just calls their Variable Valve Timing VVTL-I   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by fyerstarter (edited 06-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||06-21-2001||10:22 PM||||cant win em all. I get beat too sometimes. I never try to take them from a standing start. I try to catch them where i can shift and get rite into the power band, spool up the turbo real quick and gone before they know what hit them. Ive got better torque from 40 or so up, than at bottom. Mines def not a drag car, but fun to watch them in mirror trying to hang onto the corners behind me.||||reg||1
Z||000009||BENGAL4||06-21-2001||11:00 PM||||Watch those Bengal comments, Chadman. This time of year, we are as good as everyone else. Besides, I hope I see that Celica on my way home from Canada. 3800 II S/C in an 86GT with license plate BENGAL4. That will be one tiger with teeth and claws. I am finally getting it back. I leave on July 3 and returning July 4. E-mail me if you will be home and I will stop by as planned. Boy, you sure know how to get a rise out of me. LOL.<P>Bill||||reg||10
